**Read:** [Uncertainty quantification in particle image velocimetry — Sciacchitano](../sources/PIV-Uncertainty-Sciacchitano.lingua#r_4PHTCFRTAGSCNV1TK192VZHGQ6), the complete review and the primary uncertainty method chosen for the investigation; [Experimental Methods in Fluid Mechanics — Pranab K. Mondal](../sources/Experimental-Methods-in-Fluids-Mondal.lingua#r_4XFYEGQVB1EV4QF9BP17ME04Y4), flow visualization and micro-PIV lessons; [Fluid mechanics films and illustrated notes — NCFMF](../sources/NCFMF-Fluid-Mechanics-Films.lingua#r_0RT6J26HJJ83MX74030JPEHQVP), visualizations interpreted with their accompanying notes.

A dye line, illuminated particle sheet or schlieren image represents a particular optical and material process. Decide whether it records a trajectory, streak, concentration field or refractive-index gradient. Its apparent shape cannot be read as an instantaneous streamline without the required conditions.

For particle image velocimetry, connect seeding, particle response, illumination, calibration, imaging, timing and correlation to displacement and then velocity. Interrogation windows and overlap impose spatial filtering. Out-of-plane motion, reflections, peak ambiguity and validation/replacement choices affect the inferred field. Stereo or volumetric methods add calibration and reconstruction assumptions.

Propagate uncertainty into vorticity, strain, stresses or pressure only with the correlations and differentiation/integration method made explicit. Compare the integral of a measured profile with independent flow or force data. Publish the processing parameters and retain the unmodified measurement evidence in an appropriate external archive so a revised interpretation can be checked.

